lving Two-Step Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048673 #edb/ref 1033 66 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048673 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "b3c9ca33-97a8-546e-af44-a9a7a7a71eb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1031 "Modeling and Solving With One-Variable Linear Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1033 6417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049736 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "0f5bd25a-2d5b-5e8c-8608-1efccdd21e21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving One-Step Linear Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1033 38 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049986 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2424a53c-3dea-5c8f-aeb6-365cf563d5f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Two-Step Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1033 4021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050503 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4e9c2678-4be0-55d7-9838-e4f11d55dccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192539 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192539 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $10x - 4 > 16$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192539 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea06319a-98d8-5b73-a224-a8c03005b5db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192539 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}10x - 4 & > 16 \\\\ 10x - 4 + 4 & > 16 + 4 \\\\ 10x + 0 & > 20 \\\\ 10x & > 20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $10{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}10x & > 20 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & > \\frac{20}{10} \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & > 2 \\\\ x & > 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x> 2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192540 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12877" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192540 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $-2x + 3 > -1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192540 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1107a2bf-525e-5a08-9f28-dfd8c72718c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192540 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2x + 3 & > - 1 \\\\ -2x + 3 - 3 & > - 1 - 3 \\\\ -2x + 0 & > - 4 \\\\ -2x & > - 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2x & > - 4 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & <\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & <2 \\\\ x & <2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192541 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192541 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $-11 \\le -8y + 5$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa636b0d-3494-56b7-8be2-b634316f60ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192541 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & \\le - 8y + 5 \\\\ -11 - 5 & \\le - 8y + 5 - 5 \\\\ -16 & \\le - 8y + 0 \\\\ -16 & \\le - 8y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-8$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & \\le- 8y \\\\ \\frac{-16}{-8} & \\ge\\frac{-8y}{-8} \\\\ 2 & \\ge\\frac{-8y}{-8} \\\\ 2 & \\gey\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny \\le 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\ny \\le 2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Linear Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192842 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5fd17c91-187c-5849-9648-7b31f2b3be96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192843 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Linear Inequalities When Flipping is Required" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192843 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192843 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4cb884d3-1a4f-56aa-8628-b899f4eefacb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186192940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192844 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192844 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192844 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192844 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b6076650-101c-5fbf-bf47-9de8e6888288" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Two-Step Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186193766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192903 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "baef8b1d-be2f-50d5-a6ff-93120a166f8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193766 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193766 #edb/ref 1061 72622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193766 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8806810c-20b6-5fe2-8391-54bcad46c9c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193766 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193767 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193767 #edb/ref 1061 72623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193767 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d13e0838-e726-5176-9bda-6c3c268e6f6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193767 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193768 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193768 #edb/ref 1061 72627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193768 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a071a825-5147-5a63-8643-4bf286ad0601" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193768 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193769 #edb/ref 1061 72631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193769 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8c216a09-f324-56db-8914-490a9ba85323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193769 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193912 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wish to find the solution to the inequality\n\n$$\n2x + 6 < 12\n$$\n\nAn inequality like this one can be solved just like an equation, using the addition and multiplication principles.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $6$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x + 6 & < 12 \\\\ 2x + 6 - 6 & < 12 - 6 \\\\ 2x + 0 & < 6 \\\\ 2x & < 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x & < 6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & < \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & < 3 \\\\ x & < 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $x < 3$ In other words, any value less than $3$ satisfies the inequality.\n\nLet's see another example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193912 #edb/ref 1065 8062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193912 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0d9501dc-3e68-5741-9382-814ea643182b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193912 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
